\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Earth, with all Thy thousand voices,
\par Praise in songs the eternal King;
\par Praise His name, whose praise rejoices
\par Ears that hear and tongues that sing.
\par Lord, from each far-peopled dwelling
\par Earth shall raise the glad acclaim;
\par All shall kneel, Thy greatness telling,
\par Sing Thy praise and bless Thy name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Come and hear the wondrous story,
\par How our mighty God of old,
\par In the terrors of His glory,
\par Back the flowing billows rolled:
\par Walled within the threatening waters,
\par Free we passed the upright wave;
\par Then was joy to Israel's daughters,
\par Loud they sang His power to save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Bless the Lord, who ever liveth;
\par Sound His praise through every land,
\par Who our dying souls reviveth,
\par By whose arm upheld we stand.
\par Now upon this cheerful morrow
\par We Thine altars will adorn,
\par And the gifts we vowed in sorrow
\par Pay on joy's returning morn.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Come, each faithful soul, who fearest
\par Him who fills the eternal throne:
\par Hear, rejoicing while thou hearest,
\par What our God for us hath done;
\par When we made our supplication,
\par When our voice in prayer was strong,
\par Straight we found His glad salvation;
\par And His mercy fills our tongue.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

